OVERVIEW: Query and retrieve DICOM studies

USAGE: dicom-qr query [<options>] <host> --aet <aet>

ARGUMENTS:
  <host>                  PACS server hostname or IP address, optionally with
                          port (host:port)

OPTIONS:
  --port <port>           PACS server port (default: 11112, the registered
                          DICOM port; 104 is the well-known port — PS3.8 9.1.2)
  --aet <aet>             Local Application Entity Title (calling AE)
  --called-aet <called-aet>
                          Remote Application Entity Title (default: ANY-SCP)
                          (default: ANY-SCP)
  --move-dest <move-dest> Move Destination (0000,0600): AE Title of the Storage
                          SCP that receives the C-STORE sub-operations
                          (required for C-MOVE)
  --method <method>       Retrieval method: c-move (Study Root Query/Retrieve
                          Information Model - MOVE) or c-get (Study Root
                          Query/Retrieve Information Model - GET) (default:
                          c-move) (default: c-move)
  --patient-name <patient-name>
                          Patient's Name (0010,0010) — wildcards * and ? per
                          PS3.4 C.2.2.2.4 (case handling of PN matching is the
                          SCP's)
  --patient-id <patient-id>
                          Patient ID (0010,0020)
  --study-date <study-date>
                          Study Date (0008,0020): YYYYMMDD, or a range
                          YYYYMMDD-YYYYMMDD, -YYYYMMDD or YYYYMMDD- (PS3.4
                          C.2.2.2.5)
  --study-uid <study-uid> Study Instance UID (0020,000D)
  --accession-number <accession-number>
                          Accession Number (0008,0050)
  --modality <modality>   Modality filter (0008,0060) — e.g. CT, MR, US, OPT.
                          Run 'dicom-tags --list-modalities' for every DICOM
                          2026a code.
  --strict-modality       Reject a --modality value that is not a current DICOM
                          Defined Term
  --study-description <study-description>
                          Study Description (0008,1030) — wildcards * and ? per
                          PS3.4 C.2.2.2.4
  -o, --output <output>   Output directory for retrieved files (default: .)
  --hierarchical          Organize C-GET output hierarchically (<output>/<Study
                          Instance UID>/); C-MOVE output is stored by the move
                          destination
  --interactive           Interactive mode - select studies to retrieve
  --auto                  Automatic mode - retrieve all matching studies
  --review                Review mode - query only, save state for later
  --save-state <save-state>
                          Save query/retrieval state to file
  --timeout <timeout>     Connection timeout in seconds (default: 60) (default:
                          60)
  --parallel <parallel>   Maximum concurrent retrievals: up to N studies are
                          retrieved at once, each on its own association;
                          per-study lines are printed in study order (default:
                          1) (default: 1)
  --priority <priority>   Priority (0000,0700) of each C-MOVE-RQ / C-GET-RQ:
                          low (0002H), medium (0000H), high (0001H) — PS3.7
                          Tables 9.3-9 / 9.3-6 (default: medium) (values: low,
                          medium, high; default: medium)
  --validate              Validate retrieved files
  --transfer-syntax <transfer-syntax>
                          Requested transfer syntax for retrieved files —
                          negotiated during association setup. Accepts any
                          name/UID the shared parser understands; canonical
                          tokens: explicit-vr-le, implicit-vr-le,
                          explicit-vr-be, deflate, jpeg-baseline,
                          jpeg-extended, jpeg-lossless, jpeg-lossless-sv1,
                          jpeg2000-lossless, jpeg2000, jpeg2000-part2-lossless,
                          jpeg2000-part2, htj2k-lossless, htj2k-rpcl, htj2k,
                          jpeg-ls-lossless, jpeg-ls, jpeg-xl-lossless, jpeg-xl,
                          rle-lossless.
  --verbose               Show verbose output
  --include-parent-keys   Non-baseline: also request parent-level attributes as
                          return keys at SERIES/INSTANCE level (dicom-qr
                          queries at STUDY level, where every requested key is
                          already level-appropriate; accepted for parity with
                          dicom-query)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

